From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proton GE Team <proton-ge@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Honor autoplay when Load is requested.

AVPro's live-stream path pauses the Media Engine while preparing the source,
enables autoplay, and calls Load.  Returning E_NOTIMPL leaves the pending
pause/scrub transition without a matching play request, so AVPro eventually
reports an unknown playback error even though Media Foundation is decoding
the HLS stream.

Treat Load as a successful request and use the existing Play state machine
when autoplay is enabled.  Play already handles pending source, seek, scrub,
and pause transitions without restarting the source.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -2026,16 +2026,22 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_Load(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface)
 {
     struct media_engine *engine = impl_from_IMFMediaEngineEx(iface);
-    HRESULT hr = E_NOTIMPL;
+    BOOL autoplay = FALSE;
+    HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 
-    FIXME("(%p): stub.\n", iface);
+    TRACE("(%p).\n", iface);
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
 
     if (engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_SHUT_DOWN)
         hr = MF_E_SHUTDOWN;
+    else
+        autoplay = !!(engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_AUTO_PLAY);
 
     LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
 
+    if (autoplay)
+        hr = IMFMediaEngineEx_Play(iface);
+
     return hr;
 }
 
